# Implementation Plan: Advanced Optical + SAR Fusion Analysis System for SatVistaar-SIH

Extend the existing **SatVistaar-SIH** multimodal satellite intelligence platform with a production-grade **Optical + SAR Fusion Analysis System**. This system accepts co-registered optical/multispectral imagery and synthetic aperture radar (SAR) imagery of the same geographic area to synthesize joint multimodal intelligence that exploits complementary spectral context (vegetation, visual land cover, water color) and radar structural backscatter (surface roughness, double-bounce built structures, specular smooth water, cloud-penetrating observation).

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Zero Breaking Changes**: All 4 existing missions (`VQA`, `CAPTIONING`, `FEATURE_IDENTIFICATION`, `CHANGE_ANALYSIS`) remain 100% operational and backward-compatible. Optical + SAR Fusion will be introduced as a first-class 5th analysis mission (`OPTICAL_SAR_FUSION`) seamlessly integrated into the existing agentic pipeline, model router, and UI.

> [!NOTE]
> **Model Agnostic & Dual-Engine Fusion**:
> 1. **Python ML Specialist Engine** (`/predict/fusion`): Performs real raster processing (OpenCV/NumPy/PIL) including SAR speckle filtering, log backscatter transformation, optical NDVI/spectral proxy estimation, cross-modal agreement matrix calculation, and fusion map generation.
> 2. **Cloud/Local VLM Engine** (Groq / Ollama): Provides natural language reasoning using specialized remote-sensing fusion prompt contracts.
> 3. **Deterministic Fallback**: If the primary engine is unavailable, the system gracefully falls back while preserving the structured JSON contract.

